.TH CHECKSTYLE 1

.SH NAME
checkstyle \- Java source code style and quality checker

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B checkstyle
[\fIOPTION\fP...] \fIFILE\fP...

.SH DESCRIPTION
Checkstyle verifies that the specified source code files adhere to the specified
rules. By default, violations are reported to standard out in plain format.
Checkstyle requires a configuration XML file that configures the checks to apply.

This wrapper script intercepts parser and compilation failures
(\fIcom.puppycrawl.tools.checkstyle.api.CheckstyleException\fP) that arise
when analyzing uncompilable code, and outputs a diagnostic message
(\fICheckstyle suspects this file may not compile!\fP) in plain text or XML
format matching the requested output format.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fIFILE\fP...
One or more source files or folders to verify.

.TP
\fB-b\fP, \fB--branch-matching-xpath\fP=\fIxpath\fP
Shows Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) branches that match given XPath query.

.TP
\fB-c\fP=\fIconfigurationFile\fP
Specifies the location of the file that defines the configuration modules.
The location can either be a filesystem location, or a name passed to the
\fIClassLoader.getResource()\fP method.

.TP
\fB-d\fP, \fB--debug\fP
Prints all debug logging of CheckStyle utility.

.TP
\fB-e\fP, \fB--exclude\fP=\fIexclude\fP
Directory or file to exclude from CheckStyle. The path can be the full, absolute
path, or relative to the current path. Multiple excludes are allowed.

.TP
\fB-E\fP, \fB--executeIgnoredModules\fP
Allows ignored modules to be run.

.TP
\fB-f\fP=\fIformat\fP
Specifies the output format. Valid values: \fBxml\fP, \fBsarif\fP, \fBplain\fP for
\fIXMLLogger\fP, \fISarifLogger\fP, and \fIDefaultLogger\fP respectively. Defaults to \fBplain\fP.

.TP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--generate-xpath-suppression\fP
Generates an output xpath suppression XML to use to suppress all violations from user's config.
Instead of printing every violation, all violations will be caught and a single suppressions
xml file will be printed out. Used only with \fB-c\fP option. Output location can be
specified with \fB-o\fP option.

.TP
\fB-G\fP, \fB--generate-checks-and-files-suppression\fP
Generates an output suppression XML that will have suppress elements with "checks" and "files"
attributes only to use to suppress all violations from user's config. Instead of printing every
violation, all violations will be caught and a single suppressions xml file will be printed out.
Used only with \fB-c\fP option. Output location can be specified with \fB-o\fP option.

.TP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP
Show this help message and exit.

.TP
\fB-j\fP, \fB--javadocTree\fP
This option is used to print the Parse Tree of the Javadoc comment. The file has to contain only
Javadoc comment content excluding '/**' and '*/' at the beginning and at the end respectively.
It can only be used on a single file and cannot be combined with other options.

.TP
\fB-J\fP, \fB--treeWithJavadoc\fP
This option is used to display the Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) with Javadoc nodes of the
specified file. It can only be used on a single file and cannot be combined with other options.

.TP
\fB-o\fP=\fIoutputPath\fP
Sets the output file. Defaults to stdout.

.TP
\fB-p\fP=\fIpropertiesFile\fP
Sets the property files to load.

.TP
\fB-s\fP=\fIsuppressionLineColumnNumber\fP
Prints xpath suppressions at the file's line and column position. Argument is the line and column
number (separated by a \fB:\fP) in the file that the suppression should be generated for. The option
cannot be used with other options and requires exactly one file to run on to be specified. Note
that the generated result will have few queries, joined by pipe(\fB|\fP). Together they will match
all AST nodes on specified line and column. You need to choose only one and recheck that it works.

.TP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--tree\fP
This option is used to display the Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) without any comments of the specified
file. It can only be used on a single file and cannot be combined with other options.

.TP
\fB-T\fP, \fB--treeWithComments\fP
This option is used to display the Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) with comment nodes excluding Javadoc
of the specified file. It can only be used on a single file and cannot be combined with other options.

.TP
\fB-V\fP, \fB--version\fP
Print version information and exit.

.TP
\fB-w\fP, \fB--tabWidth\fP=\fItabWidth\fP
Sets the length of the tab character. Used only with \fB-s\fP option. Default value is 8.

.TP
\fB-x\fP, \fB--exclude-regexp\fP=\fIexcludeRegex\fP
Directory/file pattern to exclude from CheckStyle. Multiple excludes are allowed.

.SH EXAMPLES
Audit a Java source file against a custom configuration file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
$ \fBcheckstyle\fP -c /path/to/checks.xml MyClass.java
.RE
.fi
.PP
Output violations in XML format to a file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
$ \fBcheckstyle\fP -f xml -c /path/to/checks.xml -o report.xml src/
.RE
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fP
Verification succeeded and no errors or style violations were detected.
.TP
\fB>0\fP
Style violations were encountered or execution failed.

.SH SEE ALSO
